16. PUBLIC HEARING regarding a subdivision permit and plat for The
Badlands, located in a portion of Sec 34, T16N, R67W, Laramie
County, WY.
25 - 147
The Badlands, Subdivision Permit and Plat
Attachments:
Justin Arnold, Planning, said Steil Surveying Services, LLC, on behalf of Energy
Construction of WY, LLC, submitted a subdivision permit and plat application for a
portion of the NE1/4 and the S1/2 Sect 34, T16N, R67W, located north of Sunlight Rd
and east of Rd 120. He said the proposed subdivision will create 34 residential tracts
from the 349.82-acre parcel with an average of 10.29 acres.
Commissioner Zwonitzer asked about ranch waste in the area. Shane Hanson, agent,
said the applicant has agreed to clean up the property.
Arnold said based on evidence provided, staff recommends approval with the
adoption of findings of fact a and b.
Commissioner Zwonitzer asked who would maintain the cistern. Hanson said the
applicant is requesting the use of the public safety funds, and the county would
maintain the cistern. Matt Butler, County Fire Warden, confirmed that the fire district
(Laramie County Fire Authority) would maintain the cistern.
Chairman Malm opened the hearing for PUBLIC COMMENT. David Webster,
resident, expressed concerns about moving fence lines and cost of replacement.
Hearing no further PUBLIC COMMENT, Chairman Malm closed the hearing.
A motion was made by Commissioner Zwonitzer, seconded by
Commissioner Hollingshead, to approve the subdivision permit and plat for
The Badlands located in a portion of Sect 34, T16N, R67W, 6th PM,
Laramie County, WY, with one condition and adopt the findings of fact a
and b of the staff report.
Molly Bennett, Public Works, said the project will require a right-of-way permit. She
said the fence issue could be addressed during the road's design process and
