18. PUBLIC HEARING regarding a vacation and administrative plat of a
portion of Tract 5, O’Connor Ranchettes, Laramie County, WY.
25 - 154
Osvaldo Peralta Guerrero, Board Approval Vacation
and Administrative Plat, O'Connor Rachettes
Attachments:
Justin Arnold, Planning, said Jones Land Surveying, Inc, on behalf of Osvaldo Peralta
Guerrero, submitted an administrative plat application for property located in
O’Connor Ranchettes Subdivision north of the intersection of Bade Rd and Happy
Jack Rd. He said the application asks to vacate a portion of Tract 5 and subdivide it
into two parcels.
Arnold said based on evidence provided, staff recommends approval with the
adoption of findings of fact a, b and c.
Chairman Malm opened the hearing for PUBLIC COMMENT. Kevin Steiner, Eleanor
Stebbing, Scott Ellis, LaRoy Books, James Grayer and Marilyn Ellis, residents,
expressed their concerns. The concerns expressed were water, road maintenance
and traffic, increase in population density, further subdividing property, skyline view,
and dogs harassing people and cattle. Hearing no further PUBLIC COMMENT,
Chairman Malm closed the hearing.
Chairman Malm explained any further subdividing would require a subdivision permit
and plat.
A motion was made by Vice Chairman Thompson, seconded by
Commissioner Zwonitzer, that this agenda item be approved.
Commissioner Thompson spoke about the water issue and the process of creating
the AMEC memo, which divided the county into four zones for minimum lot sizes that
would not negatively impact the aquifer. He also spoke about the land use regulations,
and if an applicant follows regulations, then the board does not have basis to deny an
application.
Commissioner Heath said she understands the concerns about water. She spoke
Page 9 of 10
